{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03285",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.27,
      "end_seconds": 7.83,
      "duration_seconds": 6.56,
      "text": "All set here, doctor. Chart's updated, and I'll read the readings out when you're ready."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.85,
      "end_seconds": 15.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "Good, thank you. Welcome, tell me what's brought you in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 15.57,
      "end_seconds": 21.69,
      "duration_seconds": 6.12,
      "text": "Hmm, hello, doctor, I came in with them, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.76,
      "end_seconds": 26.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Yes, that's no problem at all. Please sit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.41,
      "end_seconds": 34.27,
      "duration_seconds": 6.86,
      "text": "Yeah, it's severe back pain. I thought I'd wait, but it hasn't gone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 36.31,
      "end_seconds": 46.51,
      "duration_seconds": 10.2,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Heart rate 88, respiratory rate 21, BP is 114 over 66. Oxygen saturation is 98 percent, temp 38.3 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.14,
      "end_seconds": 51.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.75,
      "text": "Okay, noted. When was the first time you noticed it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.62,
      "end_seconds": 66.51,
      "duration_seconds": 13.89,
      "text": "It's been about a week now. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.06,
      "end_seconds": 71.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "Is it there all the time or does it come and go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.56,
      "end_seconds": 76.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "It's, It's a few times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.82,
      "end_seconds": 80.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "Mm-hmm. Is it bearing on you a lot?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.02,
      "end_seconds": 82.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "I'd say severe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.04,
      "end_seconds": 89.66,
      "duration_seconds": 6.62,
      "text": "Mm, I was just going to say that the main thing is—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 89.76,
      "end_seconds": 96.16,
      "duration_seconds": 6.4,
      "text": "Sorry to cut in, doctor, quick question: shall I bring the trolley in now or later?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.52,
      "end_seconds": 103.06,
      "duration_seconds": 5.54,
      "text": "Later, thanks. Please go on. Have you had weakness in the legs?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.93,
      "end_seconds": 109.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "Um, uh, yes, for three weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.0,
      "end_seconds": 114.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "Okay, how much does it limit you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.44,
      "end_seconds": 122.92,
      "duration_seconds": 7.48,
      "text": "Well, it's... hard to say, it's kind of... I don't know—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.61,
      "end_seconds": 128.74,
      "duration_seconds": 5.13,
      "text": "Take your time. Mild, moderate, or severe, if you had to pick?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.72,
      "end_seconds": 131.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "Mild, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.36,
      "end_seconds": 134.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "Have you had trouble passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.88,
      "end_seconds": 144.97,
      "duration_seconds": 9.09,
      "text": "Erm, um, yes, that started yesterday. Uh, and there's a fever as well, six months now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.29,
      "end_seconds": 152.01,
      "duration_seconds": 5.72,
      "text": "Have you had severe back pain before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.47,
      "end_seconds": 160.53,
      "duration_seconds": 7.06,
      "text": "Actually, you know, a bit, last winter. It settled by itself back then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.24,
      "end_seconds": 180.39,
      "duration_seconds": 5.15,
      "text": "A few quick ones: weight loss, recent fall or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.82,
      "end_seconds": 186.34,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "I mean, uh, none of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.64,
      "end_seconds": 193.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Any rashes or skin problems otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.0,
      "end_seconds": 194.99,
      "duration_seconds": 0.99,
      "text": "Skin's normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.71,
      "end_seconds": 199.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "Let's talk a little about your daily life and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.39,
      "end_seconds": 211.17,
      "duration_seconds": 10.78,
      "text": "Nothing, I'm teetotal. I smoke roughly a pack every two days. Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.99,
      "end_seconds": 215.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 217.47,
      "end_seconds": 221.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "Kiwi. I come out in... well, hives."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.2,
      "end_seconds": 225.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 227.04,
      "end_seconds": 235.4,
      "duration_seconds": 8.36,
      "text": "I've got diabetes. I have acid reflux. I have epilepsy, for about ten years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.46,
      "end_seconds": 248.16,
      "duration_seconds": 11.7,
      "text": "Ah. Okay, yes, diabetes and acid reflux are known to us, good to have that clear. What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 249.19,
      "end_seconds": 268.68,
      "duration_seconds": 19.49,
      "text": "Uh, um, I take metformin, 500 milligrams, twice a day. So, I'm on omeprazole, 20 milligrams, once a day for the reflux. It's something called lamo... lamotrigine, 100 milligrams, maybe, twice a day for the fits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.48,
      "end_seconds": 274.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "Did you happen to bring the box or the paperwork?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 276.2,
      "end_seconds": 280.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "No, it's at home. It's injecting drugs, recent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.41,
      "end_seconds": 287.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "Now I'm going to do a short physical check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.14,
      "end_seconds": 292.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Stay as you are for a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.02,
      "end_seconds": 317.84,
      "duration_seconds": 6.82,
      "text": "Your spine is extremely tender at one level and your leg strength is reduced."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.86,
      "end_seconds": 331.71,
      "duration_seconds": 11.85,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me. Okay, thinking it through, the most likely explanation is a possible spinal infection pressing on the nerves. Another possibility is a slipped disc."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 333.64,
      "end_seconds": 337.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "Yeah, you know, will it clear up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 338.47,
      "end_seconds": 359.76,
      "duration_seconds": 21.29,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's a possible spinal infection pressing on the nerves, and we'll know more once the urgent blood tests is back. So, to recap quickly. You've had severe back pain for about a week, severe, and no weight loss or recent fall."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 363.91,
      "end_seconds": 366.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "Yes, uh, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 375.09,
      "end_seconds": 386.21,
      "duration_seconds": 11.12,
      "text": "Urgent blood tests is what I'd like next, for possible spinal infection. I'm sending you for an urgent MRI of the spine because of possible epidural abscess."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 387.82,
      "end_seconds": 388.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.13,
      "text": "Right, understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 390.79,
      "end_seconds": 414.02,
      "duration_seconds": 23.23,
      "text": "You are going to hospital now, this can cause permanent weakness. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. Do get help quickly if the symptoms get worse. We'll catch up straight away. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 414.92,
      "end_seconds": 416.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "That's clear, thanks."
    }
  ]
}